From: David J. Vandenburgh <david@vandenburgh.co>
Subject: [PATCH] tty: serial: qcom-geni: unmask the irq when suspend fails

1006 masks a non-console port's irq at the top of suspend and unmasks it
in resume. If uart_suspend_port() or pm_runtime_force_suspend() fails,
the PM core never calls resume for that device, so the irq stayed masked
and the port went deaf until reboot (on the RP6 that is the gamepad MCU).

Put the port back and unmask the irq on both suspend failure paths. The
port is resumed first: with uport->suspended still set the ISR returns
IRQ_NONE and the unmasked line would storm, which is what 1006 is there
to stop.

A failed resume unmasks it too, as PortareOS's 7.3 version of this fix
does: the next suspend masks it again, so a resume that left it masked
would disable it for good.

---
diff --git a/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c b/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
@@ -2120,7 +2120,7 @@
 
 	ret = uart_suspend_port(private_data->drv, uport);
 	if (ret)
-		return ret;
+		goto err_unmask;
 
 	/*
 	 * When no_console_suspend is set the console must remain active
@@ -2129,7 +2129,23 @@
 	if (!console_suspend_enabled && uart_console(uport))
 		return 0;
 
-	return pm_runtime_force_suspend(dev);
+	ret = pm_runtime_force_suspend(dev);
+	if (ret) {
+		uart_resume_port(private_data->drv, uport);
+		goto err_unmask;
+	}
+
+	return 0;
+
+err_unmask:
+	/*
+	 * The PM core does not call resume for a device whose suspend failed,
+	 * so the irq masked above has to come back here or the port stays
+	 * deaf until reboot.
+	 */
+	if (!uart_console(uport))
+		enable_irq(uport->irq);
+	return ret;
 }
 
 static int qcom_geni_serial_resume(struct device *dev)
@@ -2141,8 +2157,16 @@
 
 	if (console_suspend_enabled || !uart_console(uport)) {
 		ret = pm_runtime_force_resume(dev);
-		if (ret)
+		if (ret) {
+			/*
+			 * Unmask anyway, as PortareOS does: suspend masked the irq
+			 * once and the next suspend masks it again, so leaving it
+			 * masked here would disable it for good.
+			 */
+			if (!uart_console(uport))
+				enable_irq(uport->irq);
 			return ret;
+		}
 	}
 
 	ret = uart_resume_port(private_data->drv, uport);
